{"title":"1963 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problem 30","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is positive, which of the following is always less than one?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/1/2510a8bd9049275e29ed989bda36817f344d1bc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)} \\quad 1/x \\quad \\text{(B)} \\quad x^2 \\quad \\text{(C)} \\quad \\frac{x}{x+1} \\quad \\text{(D)} \\quad \\frac{1+x}{x} \\quad \\text{(E)} \\frac{1-x}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"439\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Most of the answer choices can be eliminated by selecting a number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/2/2b25d33821cc59e9d8a4a0b9bdb419f623203485.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;x&lt;1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" /> This gets rid of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/7/d172d3d8333a9c1740b123ea13d5b44f22446869.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/e/d6e13fe9c2b73f17eeec186ee2afff58c96b4612.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1-x}{x}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"49\" height=\"37\" /> \n</p><p>If you select a very large value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/0/6d0382f3585219947b495ac2262a81b7b0c40db2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> will be bigger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cdd1b53e5faf7a118222e4b7571d1e9afa0cf56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is positive, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/9/50938737e178190328ec7b06c69e0a2440cbdfdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1+x}{x}&gt;\\frac{x}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"82\" height=\"37\" /> and will always be bigger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cdd1b53e5faf7a118222e4b7571d1e9afa0cf56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>So, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/9/6e9af1dd29a71b599ad316396c7242866cd52bdc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(C)} \\quad \\frac{x}{x+1}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"102\" height=\"45\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_TMTA_High_School_Mathematics_Contests\" title=\"1963 TMTA High School Mathematics Contests\">1963 TMTA High School Mathematics Contests</a> (<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems\" title=\"1963 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems\">Problems</a>)</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"30%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problem_29\" title=\"1963 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problem 29\"> Problem 29</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"40%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=TMTA_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_Past_Problems/Solutions\" title=\"TMTA High School Mathematics Contest Past Problems/Solutions\">TMTA High School Mathematics Contest Past Problems/Solutions</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"30%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problem_31\" title=\"1963 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problem 31\">Problem 31</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017192442\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.017 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.036 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 94/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 661/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 305/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand siz